<https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/ai-in-research/#faq> a schema:FAQPage ;
    schema:inLanguage "en" ;
    schema:mainEntity [ a schema:Question ;
            schema:acceptedAnswer [ a schema:Answer ;
                    schema:text "Record the purpose, people responsible, data provenance, model and code versions, validation results and limits. Use data and model cards, an AI-use statement and a project register. Before a transfer, review roles and documentation with the institution's legal service. These are practical recommendations, not a compliance certification." ] ;
            schema:name "What should a laboratory document first?" ],
        [ a schema:Question ;
            schema:acceptedAnswer [ a schema:Answer ;
                    schema:text "Identify the provider, deployer and other actors for the actual system. For high-risk systems, Article 25 specifies circumstances in which rebranding, substantial modification or a changed intended purpose can make another actor the provider. Contracts should document roles; they do not replace the applicable statutory obligations." ] ;
            schema:name "Who is responsible when laboratory code is transferred?" ],
        [ a schema:Question ;
            schema:acceptedAnswer [ a schema:Answer ;
                    schema:text "As checked on October 23, 2026, the revised timeline provides December 2, 2027 for Annex III high-risk uses and August 2, 2028 for high-risk AI embedded in regulated products under Annex I. Other obligations have their own dates. Identify the relevant system and provision before applying a deadline." ] ;
            schema:name "Which high-risk AI deadlines should a laboratory track?" ],
        [ a schema:Question ;
            schema:acceptedAnswer [ a schema:Answer ;
                    schema:text "The exclusions depend on the system's purpose and stage, not simply on the user's status as a researcher. Article 2 covers systems specifically developed and put into service solely for scientific research, and certain pre-market research activities. Real-world testing is outside the latter exclusion. Reassess the scope before transfer or deployment." ] ;
            schema:name "Is scientific research exempt from the AI Act?" ] .

