                        <https://person.cyrilvoyant.com/#cyril-voyant> ;
                    schema:datePublished "2025-08-22" ;
                    schema:headline "A Simple Method for Quickly Estimating Solar Irradiance Forecast Errors" ;
                    schema:image "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/assets/img/85e5d66681cc.png" ;
                    schema:inLanguage "en" ;
                    schema:url "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/latest-publications-and-news/" ] ;
            schema:position 17 ],
        [ a schema:ListItem ;
            schema:item [ a schema:BlogPosting ;
                    schema:abstract "Classical metrics like RMSE (root mean squared error) evaluate forecasts as if every pixel must match perfectly in space and time. Machines optimize for that. Humans do not think that way." ;
                    schema:author <https://person.cyrilvoyant.com/#cyril-voyant> ;
                    schema:datePublished "2026-03-28" ;
                    schema:headline "From Pixels to Tolerances: Rethinking Forecast Validation with the γ-Index" ;
                    schema:image "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/assets/img/7f20ac04a02f.png" ;
                    schema:inLanguage "en" ;
                    schema:url "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/latest-publications-and-news/gamma-index-forecast-validation/" ] ;
            schema:position 7 ],
        [ a schema:ListItem ;
            schema:item [ a schema:BlogPosting ;
                    schema:abstract "LQL‑Equiv is a free & open‑source software (GNU‑based) written in MATLAB and distributed as a standalone executable, developed by Cyril Voyant & Daniel Julian. It computes voxel‑wise Equivalent Dose in 2 Gy fractions (EQD₂) and Biologically Effective Dose (BED) using a Linear‑Quadratic‑Linear (LQL) model that explicitly accounts for fraction size, overall treatment time, and cellular repopulation effects, outperforming standard LQ-based calculators." ;
                    schema:author <https://person.cyrilvoyant.com/#cyril-voyant> ;
                    schema:datePublished "2025-08-04" ;
                    schema:headline "New Release: LQL-Equiv: Open‑Source Software for Biologically Equivalent Dose Calculation in Radiotherapy" ;
                    schema:image "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/assets/img/82d8378219df.png" ;
                    schema:inLanguage "en" ;
                    schema:url "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/latest-publications-and-news/" ] ;
            schema:position 18 ],
        [ a schema:ListItem ;
            schema:item [ a schema:BlogPosting ;
                    schema:abstract "Clearsky models are widely used in solar energy for many applications such as quality control, resource assessment, satellite-base irradiance estimation and forecasting. However, their use in forecasting and nowcasting is associated with a number of challenges. Synchronization errors, reliance on the Clearsky index (ratio of the global horizontal irradiance to its cloud-free counterpart) and high sensitivity of the clearsky model to errors in aerosol optical depth at low solar elevation limit th" ;
                    schema:author [ a schema:Person ;
                            schema:name "Mohammed Asloune" ;
                            schema:sameAs "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-0183-2156" ],
                        [ a schema:Person ;
                            schema:name "Milan Despotovic" ;
                            schema:sameAs "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-3144-5945" ],
                        [ a schema:Person ;
                            schema:name "Yves-Marie Saint-Drenan" ;
                            schema:sameAs "https://orcid.org/0000-0003-1471-1092" ],
                        [ a schema:Person ;
                            schema:name "Luis Garcia-Gutierrez" ;
                            schema:sameAs "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-3480-1784" ],
                        [ a schema:Person ;
                            schema:name "Gilles Notton" ;
                            schema:sameAs "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6267-9632" ],
                        <https://person.cyrilvoyant.com/#cyril-voyant> ;
                    schema:datePublished "2025-04-11" ;
                    schema:headline "On the importance of clearsky model in short-term solar radiation forecasting" ;
                    schema:image "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/assets/img/05e996273651.jpg" ;
                    schema:inLanguage "en" ;
                    schema:url "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/latest-publications-and-news/" ] ;
            schema:position 22 ],
        [ a schema:ListItem ;
            schema:item [ a schema:BlogPosting ;
                    schema:abstract "ELECTRE brings together about fifteen laboratories, centres and institutes of the Carnot M.I.N.E.S institute around 13 research projects (2023–2026) on the electrification of uses, from materials to storage, industrial processes and the limits of electrification. Its closing workshop is on 18 November 2026, Mines Paris – PSL, Sophia Antipolis." ;
                    schema:author [ a schema:Person ;
                            schema:name "Delphine Gilges-Crampont" ;
                            schema:sameAs "https://www.idref.fr/292140282" ],
                        [ a schema:Person ;
                            schema:name "Annette Massias" ;
                            schema:sameAs "https://www.linkedin.com/in/annette-massias-46544630/" ],
                        <https://person.cyrilvoyant.com/#cyril-voyant> ;
                    schema:datePublished "2026-10-23" ;
                    schema:headline "ELECTRE, flagship project of the Carnot M.I.N.E.S institute: electrifying uses, closing workshop on 18 November 2026" ;
                    schema:image "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/assets/news/electre.png" ;
                    schema:inLanguage "en" ;
                    schema:url "https://www.cyrilvoyant.com/latest-publications-and-news/" ] ;
            schema:position 2 ],
        [ a schema:ListItem ;
            schema:item [ a schema:BlogPosting ;
                    schema:abstract "I have been appointed Visiting Professor at the Faculty of Engineering, University of Kragujevac, together with my colleague and friend Prof. Gilles Notton." ;
                    schema:author [ a schema:Person ;
                            schema:name "Gilles Notton" ;
                            schema:sameAs "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-6267-9632" ],
                        <https://person.cyrilvoyant.com/#cyril-voyant> ;
